A: You have to remember that what MSVCRT calls "OS handles" are not Win32 handles, but another layer of handles added just to confuse you. MSVCRT tries to emulate the Unix handle numbers where stdin = 0, stdout = 1, stderr = 2 and so on. Win32 handles are numbered differently and their values always happen to be a multiple of 4. Opening the pipe and getting all the handles configured properly will require getting your hands messy. Using the MSVCRT source code and a debugger is probably a requirement.

